{"name":"Kickstart Purple","hex":"#7777cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kickstart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of kick start."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of kick start."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kickstart"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kickstart (Amiga)","blocks":[{"text":"Kickstart is the bootstrap firmware of the Amiga computers developed by Commodore International. Its purpose is to initialize the Amiga hardware and core components of AmigaOS and then attempt to boot from a bootable volume, such as a floppy disk. Most Amiga models were shipped with the Kickstart firmware stored on ROM chips."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Amiga_1200_Kickstart_3.0_ROMs.jpg/330px-Amiga_1200_Kickstart_3.0_ROMs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kickstart_(Amiga)","wikidata":"Q1637801"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Kickstartdiskette-1.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Kickstartdiskette-1.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Kickstart 1.2 floppy disk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKickstartdiskette-1.2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/Kickstart1_3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/Kickstart1_3.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The default boot screen displayed under Kickstart 1.3","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKickstart1_3.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a0/Amiga_kickstart2_boot_screen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a0/Amiga_kickstart2_boot_screen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The default boot screen displayed under Kickstart 2.0, requesting that the user insert a boot disk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmiga_kickstart2_boot_screen.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg/500px-Ghent_Altarpiece_D_-_Popes_-_Bishops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org